    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2GJKDpNGp4ZJfeMjMdUzpoQ)_\n\n## What\n`org-insert-link` completes the path of a link type that has a `:complete` parameter. `sp-org-id-link` now sets one for three types, once Org is loaded:\n\n- `help:` reads a function, variable or face (`completing-read` over `obarray`).\n- `info:` reads a manual and node with `Info-read-node-name` and inserts Org's `MANUAL#NODE` form (`Top` when only a manual is given).\n- `man:` reads a page with `Man-completion-table`. It also gets a follow function (`man`), but only when Org has none for `man:`.\n\nThe literate doc has a new section, and `CHANGELOG.org` has the entry.\n\n## Not tested\nNothing was run in Emacs (none in the container). I wrote this from memory of the Org and Info APIs and did not check which of the three types the installed Org already defines.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiAJc2Qd7A97uwG84ky)_",
